1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:02,200
In the highlands of Vietnam, there's a farmer

2
00:00:02,250 --> 00:00:04,020
named Pham Xuan Lan.

3
00:00:04,170 --> 00:00:06,370
This land runs on coffee.

4
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:08,420
Vietnam is the second-biggest coffee producer

5
00:00:08,470 --> 00:00:09,730
on Earth.

6
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:12,830
But Lan has 400 other trees now.

7
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:15,410
This year, he expects them to earn him about

8
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:16,290
76,000 dollars.

9
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:19,230
If he'd stuck with coffee alone?

10
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:20,130
Roughly 10,000.

11
00:00:21,260 --> 00:00:23,700
Those trees paid for a car.

12
00:00:23,750 --> 00:00:25,450
Houses for his children.

13
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:26,480
A villa.

14
00:00:26,830 --> 00:00:28,830
"You can live okay with coffee," he told

15
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:32,550
AFP, "but it's durian that makes you rich."

16
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:34,660
And almost all of that money comes from

17
00:00:34,710 --> 00:00:35,840
one place.

18
00:00:35,990 --> 00:00:38,340
China buys around 90% of all the durians

19
00:00:38,390 --> 00:00:40,230
the world exports.

20
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:42,970
Last year it spent almost 7.5 billion dollars

21
00:00:43,020 --> 00:00:44,090
on them.

22
00:00:44,140 --> 00:00:46,300
That's nearly twelve times what it spent

23
00:00:46,350 --> 00:00:48,060
a decade earlier.

24
00:00:48,210 --> 00:00:50,890
Across Southeast Asia, farmers have replanted

25
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:53,050
around one customer's appetite.

26
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:55,900
And this year, the price is falling.

27
00:00:56,050 --> 00:00:58,770
So what happens when an entire export industry

28
00:00:58,820 --> 00:01:00,940
depends on one buyer?

29
00:01:08,237 --> 00:01:10,277
If you've never met a durian:

30
00:01:10,327 --> 00:01:13,107
it's big, it's covered in spikes, and it's

31
00:01:13,157 --> 00:01:15,177
famous for its smell.

32
00:01:15,227 --> 00:01:17,667
People either love it, or can't stand being

33
00:01:17,717 --> 00:01:19,057
in the same room.

34
00:01:19,517 --> 00:01:21,727
In China, a lot of people love it.

35
00:01:21,877 --> 00:01:24,847
In 2025, fresh durian was China's most valuable

36
00:01:24,897 --> 00:01:27,067
imported fruit.

37
00:01:27,117 --> 00:01:29,637
China brought in 1.87 million tonnes, double

38
00:01:29,687 --> 00:01:33,267
the amount of just three years earlier.

39
00:01:33,867 --> 00:01:36,917
On Douyin, China's version of TikTok, videos

40
00:01:36,967 --> 00:01:39,167
of people cracking durians open have drawn

41
00:01:39,217 --> 00:01:41,127
billions of views.

42
00:01:41,177 --> 00:01:43,937
One platform sold more than 30 million durian

43
00:01:43,987 --> 00:01:45,907
orders in a single year.

44
00:01:46,407 --> 00:01:47,937
There's even a phrase for it:

45
00:01:47,987 --> 00:01:49,457
"durian freedom."

46
00:01:49,507 --> 00:01:51,657
Being able to buy one without checking the

47
00:01:51,707 --> 00:01:52,607
price.

48
00:01:53,347 --> 00:01:55,537
But China has a problem.

49
00:01:55,587 --> 00:01:58,047
Durian barely grows there.

50
00:01:58,207 --> 00:02:00,417
The tree hates temperature swings.

51
00:02:00,467 --> 00:02:03,727
Strong winds can make it shed its leaves.

52
00:02:03,777 --> 00:02:06,887
China first tried planting durian in 1958,

53
00:02:06,937 --> 00:02:09,247
and it took until 2019 to achieve a real

54
00:02:09,297 --> 00:02:10,657
breakthrough.

55
00:02:11,207 --> 00:02:13,187
So China imports.

56
00:02:13,237 --> 00:02:16,087
And for years, nearly all of its fresh durians

57
00:02:16,137 --> 00:02:18,237
came from one country.

58
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,760
That country was Thailand.

59
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:27,420
In 2021, Thailand supplied almost 100% of

60
00:02:27,470 --> 00:02:30,360
the fresh durians China imported.

61
00:02:30,810 --> 00:02:33,680
Then, in 2022, China opened the door to

62
00:02:33,730 --> 00:02:34,790
Vietnam.

63
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:38,670
What happened next was a gold rush.

64
00:02:38,980 --> 00:02:41,960
Vietnam's durian exports were worth 180

65
00:02:42,010 --> 00:02:43,710
million dollars in 2021.

66
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:46,870
This year, they're expected to hit about

67
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:48,100
4 billion.

68
00:02:48,150 --> 00:02:52,120
The land planted with durian grew more than

69
00:02:52,170 --> 00:02:55,360
fivefold in a decade, to around 200,000

70
00:02:55,410 --> 00:02:56,770
hectares.

71
00:02:57,230 --> 00:02:59,890
Coffee farmers cut down coffee trees.

72
00:02:59,940 --> 00:03:02,140
In southern Thailand, farmers ripped out

73
00:03:02,190 --> 00:03:04,190
rubber trees to make room.

74
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:07,180
In Malaysia, so many growers switched that

75
00:03:07,230 --> 00:03:10,600
mangosteen, once the cheap fruit, now costs

76
00:03:10,650 --> 00:03:13,030
more than some premium durians.

77
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:16,530
By 2025, Vietnam had overtaken Thailand

78
00:03:16,580 --> 00:03:20,140
as China's biggest supplier by volume.

79
00:03:20,190 --> 00:03:22,400
Thailand still earned more:

80
00:03:22,450 --> 00:03:25,920
just under 4 billion dollars, against Vietnam's

81
00:03:25,970 --> 00:03:27,480
3.44 billion.

82
00:03:27,860 --> 00:03:30,530
But every gold rush has casualties.

83
00:03:31,180 --> 00:03:33,730
A farmer named Hung switched his whole farm

84
00:03:33,780 --> 00:03:35,960
from coffee to durian.

85
00:03:36,010 --> 00:03:38,460
Two years later, he couldn't meet the quality

86
00:03:38,510 --> 00:03:40,560
standards buyers demanded.

87
00:03:40,610 --> 00:03:43,570
He went back to coffee, and told AFP he

88
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:46,360
would never try durian again.

89
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:49,680
Even Lan, the farmer who got rich, still

90
00:03:49,730 --> 00:03:51,250
grows coffee.

91
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:53,440
He compares growing durian to raising a

92
00:03:53,490 --> 00:03:54,360
child:

93
00:03:54,410 --> 00:03:57,590
you can do everything right and still fail.

94
00:04:00,167 --> 00:04:01,757
Here's the next problem.

95
00:04:01,807 --> 00:04:03,897
Durian doesn't travel well.

96
00:04:04,047 --> 00:04:06,547
Export durians are usually picked before

97
00:04:06,597 --> 00:04:08,517
they're fully ripe, just so they survive

98
00:04:08,567 --> 00:04:09,737
the journey.

99
00:04:09,787 --> 00:04:12,637
Every extra hour on the road costs flavor,

100
00:04:12,687 --> 00:04:13,827
and money.

101
00:04:14,047 --> 00:04:16,607
So the supply chain got faster.

102
00:04:16,657 --> 00:04:18,117
A lot faster.

103
00:04:18,447 --> 00:04:20,997
According to Xinhua, cold-chain trains on

104
00:04:21,047 --> 00:04:23,597
the China–Laos Railway now carry Thai durians

105
00:04:23,647 --> 00:04:25,777
to Kunming in 26 hours.

106
00:04:25,827 --> 00:04:29,137
Within 48 hours, they're in more than 30

107
00:04:29,187 --> 00:04:30,967
Chinese cities.

108
00:04:31,297 --> 00:04:33,807
In peak season, the trains run six times

109
00:04:33,857 --> 00:04:36,197
a day instead of two.

110
00:04:36,247 --> 00:04:39,467
In the first four months of 2026, that railway

111
00:04:39,517 --> 00:04:42,827
carried 50,300 tonnes of durians, almost

112
00:04:42,877 --> 00:04:45,077
double the year before.

113
00:04:45,477 --> 00:04:48,447
By sea, dedicated "durian express" ships

114
00:04:48,497 --> 00:04:51,007
sail from Thailand ten times a week and

115
00:04:51,057 --> 00:04:53,847
reach southern China in four days.

116
00:04:53,897 --> 00:04:56,147
At one border port, customs clearance for

117
00:04:56,197 --> 00:04:59,007
durians dropped from four hours to fifteen

118
00:04:59,057 --> 00:04:59,957
minutes.

119
00:05:00,277 --> 00:05:01,547
The result?

120
00:05:01,597 --> 00:05:04,427
By spring 2026, Thai durians were selling

121
00:05:04,477 --> 00:05:07,997
for as little as 28 yuan a kilo at one Kunming

122
00:05:08,047 --> 00:05:09,967
wholesale market.

123
00:05:10,297 --> 00:05:13,297
The luxury fruit was becoming an everyday

124
00:05:13,347 --> 00:05:14,247
fruit.

125
00:05:16,933 --> 00:05:19,663
But speed wasn't the only pressure.

126
00:05:19,713 --> 00:05:21,773
Exporters were also under pressure to make

127
00:05:21,823 --> 00:05:23,453
the fruit look good.

128
00:05:23,813 --> 00:05:26,073
Thai growers have long treated durians with

129
00:05:26,123 --> 00:05:28,363
turmeric to keep their color.

130
00:05:28,413 --> 00:05:31,393
Some traders reportedly found a cheaper,

131
00:05:31,443 --> 00:05:33,393
faster shortcut:

132
00:05:33,443 --> 00:05:36,873
Auramine O, an industrial dye made for textiles

133
00:05:36,923 --> 00:05:38,843
and paper.

134
00:05:38,893 --> 00:05:43,023
The WHO's cancer agency lists it as a possible

135
00:05:43,073 --> 00:05:44,963
carcinogen, and China declared it non-edible

136
00:05:45,013 --> 00:05:46,603
back in 2008.

137
00:05:46,963 --> 00:05:49,033
Around the start of 2025, Chinese inspectors

138
00:05:49,083 --> 00:05:51,873
reported finding the dye in Thai durians.

139
00:05:51,923 --> 00:05:56,183
From January 10, every shipment needed lab

140
00:05:56,233 --> 00:05:59,193
reports for the dye and for cadmium, a toxic

141
00:05:59,243 --> 00:06:00,043
heavy metal.

142
00:06:00,013 --> 00:06:04,073
Large batches were turned away at the border.

143
00:06:04,563 --> 00:06:07,973
For Vietnam, the timing was brutal.

144
00:06:08,023 --> 00:06:11,423
In the first four months of 2025, its durian

145
00:06:11,473 --> 00:06:14,043
exports to China reached only about 20%

146
00:06:14,093 --> 00:06:15,453
of plan:

147
00:06:15,503 --> 00:06:19,083
around 120 to 130 million dollars, down

148
00:06:19,133 --> 00:06:22,443
from more than 500 million a year earlier.

149
00:06:23,093 --> 00:06:25,353
Thailand moved fast.

150
00:06:25,403 --> 00:06:27,533
It quickly got its own labs approved to

151
00:06:27,583 --> 00:06:30,323
run the tests, and banned exporters from

152
00:06:30,373 --> 00:06:32,633
artificially coloring their fruit.

153
00:06:32,993 --> 00:06:35,253
The lesson was simple.

154
00:06:35,303 --> 00:06:37,543
When one market buys 90% of your exports,

155
00:06:37,593 --> 00:06:41,483
its standards become your standards.

156
00:06:44,367 --> 00:06:48,057
Then, in 2026, the gold rush grew up.

157
00:06:48,207 --> 00:06:50,307
A durian tree takes five to eight years

158
00:06:50,357 --> 00:06:52,057
to reach full production.

159
00:06:52,107 --> 00:06:54,157
The trees planted during the boom started

160
00:06:54,207 --> 00:06:56,557
fruiting, and they started fruiting at the

161
00:06:56,607 --> 00:06:57,917
same time.

162
00:06:58,067 --> 00:07:00,267
Thailand's Commerce Ministry projected about

163
00:07:00,317 --> 00:07:03,357
2.07 million tonnes this year, up a third,

164
00:07:03,407 --> 00:07:06,127
with around 70% meant for export.

165
00:07:06,177 --> 00:07:10,147
Malaysia had an unusually big harvest.

166
00:07:10,197 --> 00:07:13,457
And in the first half of 2026, China imported

167
00:07:13,507 --> 00:07:16,657
about 1.07 million tonnes, up by roughly

168
00:07:16,707 --> 00:07:18,997
half from a year earlier.

169
00:07:19,677 --> 00:07:20,717
More fruit.

170
00:07:20,767 --> 00:07:22,107
Same customer.

171
00:07:22,157 --> 00:07:24,337
You can guess what happened next.

172
00:07:24,527 --> 00:07:26,807
Wholesale prices for premium Vietnamese

173
00:07:26,857 --> 00:07:29,397
and Malaysian durians fell by as much as

174
00:07:29,447 --> 00:07:31,857
half compared with last year.

175
00:07:32,297 --> 00:07:35,357
In Thailand, Hong Kong's The Standard reported,

176
00:07:35,407 --> 00:07:38,067
a deputy prime minister joined an influencer

177
00:07:38,117 --> 00:07:40,737
on a livestream to sell durians at discount

178
00:07:40,787 --> 00:07:44,427
prices, hoping to lift local demand.

179
00:07:44,477 --> 00:07:46,727
Farmers were furious.

180
00:07:46,777 --> 00:07:49,117
They said it taught buyers to expect rock-bottom

181
00:07:49,167 --> 00:07:50,377
prices.

182
00:07:50,817 --> 00:07:53,437
Vietnam's own government has now warned

183
00:07:53,487 --> 00:07:54,527
of oversupply.

184
00:07:57,703 --> 00:08:00,103
And there's one more move on the board.

185
00:08:00,253 --> 00:08:02,443
China is growing its own.

186
00:08:02,643 --> 00:08:04,893
On the island of Hainan, there are now more

187
00:08:04,943 --> 00:08:06,803
than 3,000 hectares of durian orchards.

188
00:08:06,853 --> 00:08:10,223
Growers there sell their fruit as tree-ripened,

189
00:08:10,273 --> 00:08:13,293
a direct shot at imports picked early for

190
00:08:13,343 --> 00:08:14,483
the journey.

191
00:08:15,033 --> 00:08:17,323
So should Southeast Asia panic?

192
00:08:17,563 --> 00:08:18,813
Not yet.

193
00:08:18,863 --> 00:08:21,173
In 2025, China's homegrown durians amounted

194
00:08:21,223 --> 00:08:24,853
to less than 1% of its imports, and they

195
00:08:24,903 --> 00:08:26,083
still cost more to produce.

196
00:08:26,133 --> 00:08:29,213
And a durian expert at Hainan's own agricultural

197
00:08:29,263 --> 00:08:33,353
academy told AFP that Chinese durians will

198
00:08:33,403 --> 00:08:35,613
only ever be a supplement to Southeast Asian

199
00:08:35,663 --> 00:08:36,843
ones.

200
00:08:37,273 --> 00:08:39,903
The real risk was never Hainan.

201
00:08:39,953 --> 00:08:41,123
It's the math.

202
00:08:43,767 --> 00:08:46,577
For a decade, the durian boom ran on one

203
00:08:46,627 --> 00:08:47,647
assumption:

204
00:08:47,697 --> 00:08:50,357
China would always want more.

205
00:08:50,627 --> 00:08:52,907
So far, China is still buying more than

206
00:08:52,957 --> 00:08:53,757
ever.

207
00:08:53,727 --> 00:08:56,297
But when one market takes around 90% of

208
00:08:56,347 --> 00:08:59,137
global exports, it has enormous influence

209
00:08:59,187 --> 00:09:02,907
over prices, standards and speed.

210
00:09:03,267 --> 00:09:05,757
Some early growers made fortunes.

211
00:09:05,807 --> 00:09:08,217
Newer orchards are reaching maturity just

212
00:09:08,267 --> 00:09:10,127
as prices begin to soften.

213
00:09:10,507 --> 00:09:12,507
Lan seems to understand this.

214
00:09:12,557 --> 00:09:15,237
That's why, next to 400 durian trees, he

215
00:09:15,287 --> 00:09:17,137
still keeps his coffee.

216
00:09:17,357 --> 00:09:19,507
But durian isn't the only product where

217
00:09:19,557 --> 00:09:21,707
one place supplies the world.

218
00:09:21,857 --> 00:09:24,957
In one small Chinese town, they make a third

219
00:09:25,007 --> 00:09:27,447
of all the socks on the planet.

220
00:09:27,787 --> 00:09:29,077
That's the next video.

221
00:09:29,127 --> 00:09:31,167
Subscribe so you don't miss it.
